// Events keyed by wallet ID, read with the address under each field's address-era name.
//
// Most events carry the player's uint32 wallet ID, often under a new name (`walletId`, `playerId`,
// `id`, …), while the chain projections read the address under the field's address-era name. The
// event readers (facts.js eventFacts, event-store.js cachedEvents/previousEvents, client.events,
// feeds.js gameReceipt) pass decoded rows through decorateWalletRows(): it puts the resolved
// lowercase ADDRESS back under that name, and keeps the ID under its own name (or `<name>Id` when
// the name is the same, e.g. `player` -> `player` + `playerId`). Topic filters given under the
// address name with an address value are translated to the ID topic (translateWalletFilters).
//
// ID_FIELDS lists, per contract and event, [position, address name, ID name, is-array].
